From b6ba106d0de1ecb5a2643d96c3151bbbc8c71694 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Huang <sixthshifts@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:50:44 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(overlay)!: toasts open from a store; useToast takes
 its content at open time

A toast reports what an action produced, so its content is known when
it fires, not when a component renders. useToast(props) had it the
other way round: one toast per hook call, content fixed up front, and
nothing outside a component could open one at all.

The stack is now a store outside React (toastStore.ts): toast(options)
opens one from anywhere and returns a handle; useToast() returns
openToast(options), closeToast(id) and closeAllToasts() bound to the
provider's store. ToastStack renders it, owns the dismissal timer, and
drives the exit through a new open prop on Toast, so expiry and the X
button take the same animated path. The stack holds at most three, and
a danger toast has no timer unless given one. OverlayProvider takes
toasts (a store) and toastClassName (to move the stack).

BREAKING CHANGE: useToast no longer takes props; call openToast(options)
with them instead, and read the toast's id from the returned handle.
useOverlayContext().toastStack is now toastStore.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
