diff --git a/docs/overlay-primitives.md b/docs/overlay-primitives.md
index 93f5336..35de3e2 100644
--- a/docs/overlay-primitives.md
+++ b/docs/overlay-primitives.md
@@ -62,10 +62,10 @@ const toastRoot = document.getElementById("toast-root");
 It owns three things no individual overlay should:
 
 - **Two portal roots.** `modal-root` and `toast-root` are real DOM nodes in `index.html`; the provider falls back to `document.body` if either is absent (`OverlayContext.tsx:31`).
-- **Two stacks.** A `useStack` (`src/hooks/useStack.ts`) each for modals and toasts. `useModal().openModal(Component)` pushes onto the modal stack; `useToast()` pushes onto the toast stack. Stack items carry their own `onClose` and live `data` (updatable via `update()`).
+- **Two stacks, of two kinds.** Modals are a `useStack` (`src/hooks/useStack.ts`) in React state: `useModal().openModal(Component)` pushes onto it, and items carry their own `onClose` and live `data` (updatable via `update()`). Toasts are a **store outside React** (`src/lib/contexts/OverlayContext/toastStore.ts`): `toast(options)` opens one from anywhere — a store, a timer, a service-worker callback — and `useToast().openToast(options)` is the same door from inside a component. The provider renders the store through `ToastStack`. The content is given at open time, not at hook time, because a toast reports what an action produced.
 - **Global Escape for the modal stack.** A single `keydown` listener closes the *topmost* modal only — correct stack ordering, handled in one place rather than racing N per-component listeners (`OverlayContext.tsx:41`). This is why `Modal` sets `escapeKey: false` on its `useDismiss`. Trigger-anchored overlays are *not* in this stack, so they keep floating-ui's own escape dismissal; `Sheet` likewise keeps `escapeKey: true` because it's rendered inline, not via the stack.
 
-Toasts render inside the provider's own positioned container (`fixed bottom-6 left-1/2 z-toast …`), which is why a stacked `Toast` is passed `standalone={false}` — the provider positions it, the toast just animates (`OverlayContext.tsx:81`, `src/components/Toast/Toast.tsx:104`).
+Toasts render inside `ToastStack`'s positioned container (`fixed bottom-6 left-1/2 z-toast …`, overridable through the provider's `toastClassName`), which is why a stacked `Toast` is passed `standalone={false}` — the stack positions it, the toast just animates. The stack also owns the dismissal timer: on expiry it flips the toast's `open` to `false`, `Toast` plays its exit through `usePresence`, and `onClose` drops the record — the same path the X button takes, so nothing is ever unmounted mid-fade. The stack holds at most three (`createToastStore({ max })`), and a `danger` toast has no timer unless given one.
 
 ## Compound assembly
 
